{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From"},{"title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondRef"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformingTypes"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"CondProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","roleHeading":"Protocol","title":"CondProtocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CondProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:4GLib12CondProtocolP"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/condprotocol"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/broadcast()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/clear()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/free()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/init_()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/signal()","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/timedWait(mutex:absTime:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/wait(mutex:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/waitUntil(mutex:endTime:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CondProtocol","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:4GLib14PointerWrapperP","text":"PointerWrapper","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Consider the following example of a shared variable.  One or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"threads can wait for data to be published to the variable and when","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"another thread publishes the data, it can signal one of the waiting","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"threads to wake up to collect the data."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is an example for using GCond to block a thread until a condition"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is satisfied:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(C Language Example):","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["  gpointer current_data = NULL;","  GMutex data_mutex;","  GCond data_cond;","","  void","  push_data (gpointer data)","  {","    g_mutex_lock (&data_mutex);","    current_data = data;","    g_cond_signal (&data_cond);","    g_mutex_unlock (&data_mutex);","  }","","  gpointer","  pop_data (void)","  {","    gpointer data;","","    g_mutex_lock (&data_mutex);","    while (!current_data)","      g_cond_wait (&data_cond, &data_mutex);","    data = current_data;","    current_data = NULL;","    g_mutex_unlock (&data_mutex);","","    return data;","  }"],"syntax":"C"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Whenever a thread calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pop_data()"},{"type":"text","text":" now, it will wait until"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"current_data is non-","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":", i.e. until some other thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"has called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"push_data()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The example shows that use of a condition variable must always be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"paired with a mutex.  Without the use of a mutex, there would be a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"race between the check of "},{"code":"current_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by the while loop in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pop_data()"},{"text":" and waiting. Specifically, another thread could set","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"current_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" after the check, and signal the cond (with nobody"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"waiting on it) before the first thread goes to sleep. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifically useful for its ability to release the mutex and go"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to sleep atomically."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is also important to use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_cond_wait()"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_cond_wait_until()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions only inside a loop which checks for the condition to be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"true.  See ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_cond_wait()"},{"text":" for an explanation of why the condition may","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not be true even after it returns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is allocated in static storage then it can be used","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without initialisation.  Otherwise, you should call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_cond_init()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it and ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_cond_clear()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when done.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond"},{"type":"text","text":" should only be accessed via the g_cond_ functions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol exposes the methods and properties of an underlying "},{"code":"GCond","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"The default implementation of these can be found in the protocol extension below."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"For a concrete class that implements these methods and properties, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondRef"},{"type":"text","text":" as a lighweight, "},{"code":"unowned","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reference if you already have an instance you just want to use."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" struct is an opaque data structure that represents a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"condition. Threads can block on a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond"},{"text":" if they find a certain","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condition to be false. If other threads change the state of this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"condition they signal the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","isActive":true},{"text":", and that causes the waiting","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"threads to be woken up.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/CondProtocol/broadcast()":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"broadcast()","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/condprotocol\/broadcast()","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/broadcast()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"broadcast","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"If threads are waiting for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cond"},{"type":"text","text":", all of them are unblocked."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If no threads are waiting for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cond"},{"text":", this function has no effect.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"It is good practice to lock the same mutex as the waiting threads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while calling this function, though not required."}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/CondProtocol/clear()":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"clear()","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/condprotocol\/clear()","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/clear()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"clear"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Frees the resources allocated to a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"g_cond_init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/CondProtocol/wait(mutex:)":{"title":"wait(mutex:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/CondProtocol\/wait(mutex:)","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/condprotocol\/wait(mutex:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"wait"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutexT","kind":"genericParameter"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"text":"mutex","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"MutexT","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Atomically releases "},{"code":"mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and waits until "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cond"},{"type":"text","text":" is signalled."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When this function returns, "},{"code":"mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is locked again and owned by the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calling thread."}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/Cond":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Cond"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Cond","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Cond"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data structure that represents a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condition. Threads can block on a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if they find a certain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condition to be false. If other threads change the state of this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"condition they signal the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond"},{"type":"text","text":", and that causes the waiting"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"threads to be woken up.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/cond"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/PointerWrapper":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PointerWrapper"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Protocol for GLib types that wrap pointers.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/pointerwrapper","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PointerWrapper","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PointerWrapper","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","title":"GLib","abstract":[],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/CondProtocol":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","type":"reference"},{"text":" struct is an opaque data structure that represents a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condition. Threads can block on a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if they find a certain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condition to be false. If other threads change the state of this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"condition they signal the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Cond","type":"reference"},{"text":", and that causes the waiting","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"threads to be woken up."}],"url":"\/documentation\/glib\/condprotocol","kind":